  "description": "A re-entry with OPTIONI '1x', which is the only input that reaches the first term of the guard at app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl:127, WS-OPTION IS NOT NUMERIC. Byte 2 is not a space so the scan stops at WS-IDX 2, both bytes cross the JUST RIGHT move unchanged, the INSPECT replaces no space, and line 124's MOVE WS-OPTION-X TO WS-OPTION sends PIC X(02) to PIC 9(02) at equal widths - so the two characters cross unchanged and WS-OPTION really does come to hold '1x'. That is what gives IS NOT NUMERIC something to detect, and it is why OPTIONO echoes '1x' rather than a digit pair. The second and third terms are never evaluated on this input.",
